.TH SYS_VM_STATS 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_vm_stats \- retrieve virtual memory summary statistics
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_vm_stats(sys_vmstat_t *" stats ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_vm_stats ()
fills
.I *stats
with a VM and swap summary, including total/free/available memory and swap
capacity/free values.
.PP
The `sys_vmstat_t` structure includes:
- `total`, `free`, `available`
- `buffers`, `cached`
- `swap_total`, `swap_free`, `swap_cached`
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.
On error, a negative value is returned by the current implementation.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EFAULT
The supplied user pointer is invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysinfo (2),
.BR pmap_stats (2),
.BR mmap (2)
